---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About — Fantasy World Cup Draft Simulator"
  description="World Cup Draft Simulator is a free browser game where you draft a fantasy World Cup XI from 100+ historical squads (1970-2026) and run them through a simulated knockout tournament."
>

<main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
      About
    </p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl">
        What is the Fantasy Football World Cup Draft Simulator?
      </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-secondary">
      World Cup Draft Simulator is a free, browser-based fantasy football game
      and the fantasy football world cup experience built for fans who love
      World Cup history. It is the world cup dream team builder for anyone who
      wants to draft a dream XI from the semifinalists of every World Cup from
      1970 to 2026 — Pelé's Brazil 1970, Zidane's France 1998, Messi's Argentina
      2022 and more — then run that squad through a simulated group stage and
      knockout tournament against the all-time greats. Think of it as a soccer
      simulator, a football draft simulator and a world cup fantasy game rolled
      into one free browser soccer game: you pick a formation, draft your
      players, and the match engine simulates the cup with penalties and all. In
      the US it often shows up as a soccer draft game, an online soccer game or a
      free soccer simulation game, while internationally it is the fantasy soccer
      draft players return to. There is no download and no sign-up, so it is the
      easiest interactive soccer simulator to open between matches. Whether you
      call it a world cup simulator, a soccer game no download, or simply the
      world cup fantasy game, the promise is the same: build the team of your
      imagination and watch the app simulate the result you designed.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">What makes it tick</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">100+ historical squads.</strong> Every team
        is rated on the same player-stat scheme — reflexes, tackling, passing,
        finishing and more — so your picks and the AI opponents are compared
        fairly.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">A real match engine.</strong> Matches are
        simulated segment by segment with possession, shots, shot quality,
        extra time and penalty shootouts, tuned against real World Cup
        scorelines.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">Chemistry matters.</strong> Drafting
        same-nation players boosts their performance, rewarding coherent squads
        over pure stat-stacking.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">The greatest teams, at your fingertips</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      Part of the fun is rebuilding the best world cup team of all time, and the
      squad pool is built for exactly that. It is packed with greatest world cup
      teams — Brazil 1970 and their fluid attacking empire, Netherlands 1974 and
      total football, Argentina 1978, Italy 1982, France 1982, West Germany
      through the eighties, Argentina 1986 and the genius of Maradona, Italy
      1990, Brazil 1994, France 1998 and Zidane's midfield, Brazil 2002 and the
      three R's, Germany 2002, Italy 2006, Spain 2010 and tiki-taka, Germany
      2014 and a relentless machine, France 2018, and Messi's Argentina 2022.
      Every one of those names is a draftable player inside the simulator, so the
      roster you build is literally composed of the world cup winners, top
      scorers and best players of five decades. That is what makes this a world
      cup fantasy game with real substance: you are not picking cards, you are
      picking Pelé, Maradona, Zidane and Messi and placing them where they
      belong on the pitch. Because the soccer simulator respects positions and
      chemistry, you can pit Maradona's Argentina against Messi's, or line up
      Brazil 1970 against France 2022, and the match engine will simulate the
      contest inside the app rather than leave it to message-board debate. The
      2026 squads extend the pool with predicted lineups, so the greatest teams
      conversation now includes who might join the list. For a fantasy soccer
      draft this is the closest thing to coaching the all-time greats, and for a
      football draft simulator it is the reason no two tournaments play the same.
      Build the team of your imagination, lean on chemistry, and let the free
      browser soccer game decide which of the greatest world cup teams you
      assembled actually lifts the trophy.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <p>
        Under the hood, World Cup Draft Simulator is a focused football
        simulator with three systems working together. First, the squad library
        holds 100+ historical squads, every one rated on the same player-stat
        scheme — reflexes, tackling, passing, finishing, pace and vision — so
        your picks and the AI opponents are always compared on a level scale.
        That is what lets a Brazil 1970 forward line and a Germany 2014 back line
        meet fairly inside the same world cup simulation. Second, a real match
        engine simulates each game segment by segment, modelling possession,
        shots, shot quality and momentum, then resolving extra time and a
        penalty shootout simulator when a knockout tie is level. The engine is
        tuned against the shape of real World Cup scorelines so results feel
        believable without copying any actual match. Third, a chemistry model
        rewards coherent squads: drafting same-nation players boosts their
        performance, so a thoughtful world cup dream team builder beats a pile of
        stats. Together these systems make the app a soccer simulator you can
        trust to be close, a football draft simulator that respects balance, and
        a world cup fantasy game where the draft matters more than the ratings on
        paper. It is also why players describe it as an interactive soccer
        simulator and a fantasy soccer draft rather than a random generator — the
        outcome is earned by the team you assemble, not handed to you. Open the
        browser soccer game, build a squad, and the engine does the rest.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">A note on the data</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      Squads are drawn from World Cup semifinalists from 1970 to 2026, which is
      what gives the football simulator its depth. The 2026 rosters are
      fictional or predicted lineups, included so you can run a world cup
      simulator 2026 draw today rather than wait for the real event. Every
      player rating is a game-specific estimate built for simulation balance, not
      an official statistic, and the numbers are tuned so matches stay close and
      the draft matters more than any single rating. We use real player names,
      team names and tournament references for editorial and descriptive
      purposes only; they remain the property of their respective owners, and
      registered trademarks such as FIFA, EA Sports and Football Manager are not
      affiliated with this app and never appear in its branding or domain. That
      separation matters: World Cup Draft Simulator is a fantasy soccer draft and
      an interactive soccer simulator inspired by World Cup history, not a
      product tied to any governing body. The squads you draft are a celebration
      of the sport's greatest teams, presented as content you can put on the
      pitch and simulate. Because the data is editorial, the free soccer
      simulation game can include five decades of semifinalists without claiming
      to be an official record. If a rating looks generous or harsh, it is there
      to make your tournament competitive, not to settle a trivia argument. In
      short, the world cup fantasy game treats history as a roster and lets the
      match engine — not the record books — decide who wins when Brazil 1970
      meets France 2022 inside the browser soccer game you opened on a whim.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      Questions, feedback or bug reports? The fastest way to reach the team
      behind World Cup Draft Simulator is the contact page, where you can send a
      message about anything — a squad that feels mis-rated, a match that swung
      too hard, a feature you wish the soccer simulator had, or just a draft you
      are proud of. Because this is a free browser soccer game built by fans of
      the World Cup, listener feedback shapes the roadmap: formation tweaks,
      new historical squads, chemistry tuning and extra replay options all start
      as notes from players. If you are working on a world cup dream team builder
      of your own, or you run a community that loves a fantasy soccer draft, we
      are happy to compare notes on how a football draft simulator should treat
      historical data. You can also use the contact page to report a broken save
      or a bug in the penalty shootout simulator, and to suggest nations or
      years you would like added to the pool. We read every message, even when
      the inbox is busy around a real tournament, because the goal is a world
      cup fantasy game that keeps getting better with each season. There is no
      account to manage and no download to reinstall, so getting help is as
      simple as opening the online soccer game, playing a round, and telling us
      what you would change. <a class="text-mint underline" href="/contact">Get in touch</a> and
      help shape the next build of this interactive soccer simulator.
    </p>
  </section>
</main></Layout>
